<title>USA: Luby's share net falls to $0.41 in Q3.</title>
<headline>Luby's share net falls to $0.41 in Q3.</headline>
<dateline>SAN ANTONIO 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended  Nine months Ended</p>
<p>					     May 31	  May 31</p>
<p>					1997     1996     1997     1996</p>
<p> Sales			  $127,630 $117,132 $368,747 $334,304</p>
<p>Income before income taxes</p>
<p>				    14,581   17,518   40,112   46,096</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes  4,998    6,554   13,959   17,245</p>
<p> Net income			9,583   10,964   26,153   28,851</p>
<p> Net income per share	   0.41     0.46     1.12     1.23</p>
<p>Average number of shares outstanding</p>
<p>				    23,366   23,887   23,453   23,548</p>
<p>				 (In thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>Source  Luby's</p>
<p>NOTE: The company's full name is Luby's Cafeterias Inc. Luby's expensed $2.5 million in start-up costs for 25 new cafeterias through its third quarter ended May 31, causing net income for the nine-month period to be 10-1/2 cents per share lower than in the previous period, the company said on Thursday.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610 --))</p>
